" style=3D"padding-bottom: 133.333%;"><img alt=3D"Welcome to Boulder. This =
is my community, these are my people. When I come down to walk, I am amazed=
 by the immeasurable strength of these people who come to walk every weeken=
d for the hostages. And the difference they are making is palpable.=20

When I walk, I make sure to look everyone we pass in the eyes, I want them =
to have to see my face and reckon with what we=E2=80=99re fighting for. I l=
isten to the conversations that they have as we pass=E2=80=94a kid asking w=
hy these people were kidnapped and a mother struggling to find the words; w=
hispers of heartbreak; a solemn nod of support. In Boulder, our impact may =
be small, but it=E2=80=99s measurable. Every conversation started is a posi=
tive impact to which we have and will continue to contribute. Today, I brin=
g that spirit with me, the spirit of Boulder, in hopes that I can share it =
with the world from wherever I am. =F0=9F=AB=B6=20

