t=3D"Trail Details BELOW =E2=AC=87=EF=B8=8F =F0=9F=8C=B2=F0=9F=A5=BE

This is genuinely one of the most beautiful places I=E2=80=99ve ever been. =
Walking through beargrass in Glacier National Park is like something out of=
 a Dr. Seuss book or Harry Potter, it=E2=80=99s like nothing I=E2=80=99ve e=
ver seen before.=20

Glacier as a whole has so much to offer and I saw so little of it on this s=
hort escapade. Planning my trip back as soon as I can!

=F0=9F=8C=B2=F0=9F=A5=BE TRAIL: Siyeh Pass from Piegan Pass TH

Distance: 10.4mi, one-way

Description: Start at Siyeh Bend on Going-to-the-Sun Road. If you=E2=80=99r=
e coming from West Glacier make sure to purchase your timed entry to the ro=
ad the night before. Parking fills up quick so be sure to get there early.=
=20

Once you=E2=80=99re on the trail, you=E2=80=99ll follow a creek up most of =
the first leg, walking through large pine forests and beautiful meadows. As=
 you come above treeline, the view opens up. You can see Jackson Glacier be=
hind you and glacial lakes down below.=20

There=E2=80=99s a switchback that isn=E2=80=99t marked the best as you reac=
h the top of the pass, you=E2=80=99ll know you went the wrong way if you en=
d up at a snowfield=E2=80=94you don=E2=80=99t need to scramble or cross sno=
w, both of which we tried to do. Turn back and you=E2=80=99ll see the real =
path up the pass.=20

Coming down, you will see waterfalls with St. Mary=E2=80=99s lake in the di=
stance. Steep switchbacks to start and then the trail flattens out for the =
last few miles. The trail ends at Sunrift Gorge TH on Going-to-the-Sun Road=
 and you can take the shuttle back to your car!=20

Make sure to pack your bear spray and practice trail safety, there are defi=
nitely grizzlies around.=20

Can=E2=80=99t wait to see your pictures!

